@page rh="THE PARISH HOUSEHOLD · EDEN · VOICE" m="TKC: DR3 · TR · WR 6–10 · WR 33–37"
# Her voice
rec:
On the page | "They let me through the door. Figured the floor came with it." (DR3)
To the Heir | Asked why she entered, she says she wants access to the kind of power that changes things, plainly, without theology, and watches what he does with it. "Most candidates tell me they feel called." "I know." (TR)
The rules | Eden narrates only what she knows, sees, hears, suspects or feels in the moment. She notices behavior before meaning, and her silence always does work (WR 6–10). She never "had no answer" (WR).
With Judah | Attention before desire. She doesn't talk to him in a watched room, and she doesn't understand him early (WR 33–35).
