# What she already does
A character reads as one continuous person when a gesture comes back changed. The left column is already on the page in Draft Three.
tab:
| On the page | What it establishes |
| Her toe exactly behind the gold tile, and the line about the floor | She tests a limit with her body, then answers with the fewest words that work |
| The nail in her stocking, and she stays put | She'll absorb pain before she gives up position, and keeps the cost private |
| The bottom of the board first | Her ambition is defensive before it's aspirational |
| Ten of eleven dollars, and the same shoes home | She pays in advance, alone, and doesn't announce it |
| The lilies, the tripod moving two feet left, Bell watching the officials | Her intelligence lives in what she catalogs |
